{
  "about": "Kannada glossary for drharshmaheshwari.com. Every Kannada translation must use these terms: tests/i18n.test.mjs checks that when an English text contains a term, its Kannada has one of the accepted forms (a substring match, so most entries are stems that every inflection contains: ಬೊಜ್ಜ covers ಬೊಜ್ಜು, ಬೊಜ್ಜಿನ, ಬೊಜ್ಜನ್ನು). Change a term here, then retranslate what uses it. docs/translation.md has the rules.",
  "register": "Everyday spoken Kannada that a family in Bengaluru or Mysuru would use, not heavy Sanskritised (grānthika) Kannada. Common English health words that people say in Kannada stay as they are said, in Kannada script (BMI, ಬ್ಲಡ್ ಶುಗರ್, ಡಯಾಬಿಟಿಸ್, ಡಾಕ್ಟರ್, ಫ್ಯಾಟಿ ಲಿವರ್). Short sentences, polite plural (ನೀವು, ಮಾಡಿ). Numbers in 0-9, never Kannada digits. Units as in English (cm, kg). Vigorous = ತೀವ್ರ; moderate = ಮಧ್ಯಮ; energetic (moderate to vigorous) = ಚುರುಕಾದ, never ತೀವ್ರ alone.",
